&lt;/div&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Authoring Redaction History</title><link>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-redaction-history/</link><pubDate>Sun, 03 Aug 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Nainai</dc:creator><guid>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-redaction-history/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="redaction-history"&gt;Redaction History&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm supports redaction history for tracking changes to your content over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="enabling-history"&gt;Enabling History&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;History is enabled by default. To disable it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;disableHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="redaction-syntax"&gt;Redaction Syntax&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use strikethrough syntax to redact content:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;~~This text is redacted~~
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;This text is visible.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="history-display"&gt;History Display&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The redaction history appears in the contentinfo section of each page, showing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous versions of redacted content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timestamps of changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edit history from Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="customizing-history"&gt;Customizing History&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can control the display of history elements:&lt;/p&gt;</description><content:encoded>&lt;h2 id="redaction-history"&gt;Redaction History&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm supports redaction history for tracking changes to your content over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="enabling-history"&gt;Enabling History&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;History is enabled by default. To disable it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;disableHistory&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="redaction-syntax"&gt;Redaction Syntax&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use strikethrough syntax to redact content:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-markdown" data-lang="markdown"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;~~This text is redacted~~
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;This text is visible.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="history-display"&gt;History Display&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The redaction history appears in the contentinfo section of each page, showing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous versions of redacted content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timestamps of changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edit history from Git&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="customizing-history"&gt;Customizing History&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can control the display of history elements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;coffeeStat&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unifiedFooter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;coffeeStat&lt;/code&gt; — Shows a coffee consumption counter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;unifiedFooter&lt;/code&gt; — Merges license, footer menu, and coffee stat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content:encoded></item><item><title>Authoring Terms Entry</title><link>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-terms-entry/</link><pubDate>Wed, 21 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Nainai</dc:creator><guid>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-terms-entry/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="terms-entry"&gt;Terms Entry&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terms entries provide metadata for taxonomy pages (tags, categories, series, stages, authors).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="creating-a-terms-entry"&gt;Creating a Terms Entry&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a directory for your term with an &lt;code&gt;_index.md&lt;/code&gt; file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;content/tags/my-tag/_index.md
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h3 id="terms-entry-frontmatter"&gt;Terms Entry Frontmatter&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;My Custom Tag&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;A description of this tag&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;This&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;shown&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tag&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="custom-taxonomies"&gt;Custom Taxonomies&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm supports custom taxonomies. Define them in your config:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;taxonomies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;series&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;stage&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;author&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;author&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="stage-taxonomy"&gt;Stage Taxonomy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;stage&lt;/code&gt; taxonomy provides visual indicators for content lifecycle:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;seedling&lt;/code&gt; — New content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;budding&lt;/code&gt; — Growing content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;evergreen&lt;/code&gt; — Established content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create stage entries:&lt;/p&gt;</description><content:encoded>&lt;h2 id="terms-entry"&gt;Terms Entry&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terms entries provide metadata for taxonomy pages (tags, categories, series, stages, authors).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="creating-a-terms-entry"&gt;Creating a Terms Entry&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a directory for your term with an &lt;code&gt;_index.md&lt;/code&gt; file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;content/tags/my-tag/_index.md
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h3 id="terms-entry-frontmatter"&gt;Terms Entry Frontmatter&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;My Custom Tag&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;A description of this tag&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;This&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;shown&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tag&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;listing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="custom-taxonomies"&gt;Custom Taxonomies&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hugo-brewm supports custom taxonomies. Define them in your config:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;taxonomies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;series&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;series&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;stage&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;author&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;author&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="stage-taxonomy"&gt;Stage Taxonomy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;stage&lt;/code&gt; taxonomy provides visual indicators for content lifecycle:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;seedling&lt;/code&gt; — New content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;budding&lt;/code&gt; — Growing content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;evergreen&lt;/code&gt; — Established content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create stage entries:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Seedling&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;emoji&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;🌱&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="author-taxonomy"&gt;Author Taxonomy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Author entries can include biographical information:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Author Name&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;flair&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;Software Engineer&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;brief&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;biography&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;the&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;author&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;goes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</content:encoded><category>Authoring</category></item><item><title>Authoring Fullscreen Content</title><link>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-fullscreen-content/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jan 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Nainai</dc:creator><guid>https://npujol.github.io/en/post/authoring-fullscreen-content/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="fullscreen-content"&gt;Fullscreen Content&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages display content without any header, footer, or navigation elements. They occupy the entire viewport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="creating-fullscreen-pages"&gt;Creating Fullscreen Pages&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;type: 'fullscreen'&lt;/code&gt; in your frontmatter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;fullscreen&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Fullscreen Page Title&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="use-cases"&gt;Use Cases&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages are ideal for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presentations&lt;/strong&gt; — Display content without distractions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Showcases&lt;/strong&gt; — Highlight specific work or projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Articles&lt;/strong&gt; — Focus readers on the content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gallery pages&lt;/strong&gt; — Display images without UI elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="fullscreen-example"&gt;Fullscreen Example&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fullscreen page can contain any valid Markdown or HTML content. The theme ensures the content is properly centered and readable.&lt;/p&gt;</description><content:encoded>&lt;h2 id="fullscreen-content"&gt;Fullscreen Content&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages display content without any header, footer, or navigation elements. They occupy the entire viewport.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="creating-fullscreen-pages"&gt;Creating Fullscreen Pages&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;type: 'fullscreen'&lt;/code&gt; in your frontmatter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-toml" data-lang="toml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;fullscreen&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;Fullscreen Page Title&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;---&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="use-cases"&gt;Use Cases&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fullscreen pages are ideal for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Presentations&lt;/strong&gt; — Display content without distractions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Showcases&lt;/strong&gt; — Highlight specific work or projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Articles&lt;/strong&gt; — Focus readers on the content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gallery pages&lt;/strong&gt; — Display images without UI elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="fullscreen-example"&gt;Fullscreen Example&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A fullscreen page can contain any valid Markdown or HTML content. The theme ensures the content is properly centered and readable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fullscreen pages are accessible via direct links or from slides with &lt;code&gt;target&lt;/code&gt; parameters.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content:encoded><category>Authoring</category></item></channel></rss>